The bug was caused by the `SamplingAccumulator` returning inconsistent labels when aggregating results for non-existing categories. Specifically, when a category was not found, the accumulator would still attempt to label the result, leading to incorrect labeling and potentially misleading output. The modifications ensure that if a category does not exist, an empty result is added instead of attempting to label it.

